# Salesforce API Notes

## `ValidationRule.Metadata` is one record at a time

The `Metadata` field holds `errorConditionFormula`, but Salesforce refuses to return it
for multi-record queries. Query ids first, then retrieve each rule individually.

```python
# BAD — errors when the object has more than one rule
"SELECT Id, ValidationName, Metadata FROM ValidationRule"

# GOOD — two passes
ids = tooling_query(
    "SELECT Id, ValidationName, Active, ErrorMessage, ErrorDisplayField "
    "FROM ValidationRule WHERE EntityDefinition.QualifiedApiName = 'Opportunity'"
)
for rule in ids:
    detail = tooling_get(f"sobjects/ValidationRule/{rule['Id']}")  # has Metadata
```

## Endpoints

- Tooling query: `/services/data/v{VERSION}/tooling/query/?q={soql}`
- Describe: `/services/data/v{VERSION}/sobjects/{object}/describe`
- Pin `VERSION` in config. Do not let it float.

## Read-only means read-only

Only `GET` against the org, plus the `POST` to the token endpoint.
`ValidationRule` supports `create()`/`update()` — never call them.

## Other gotchas

- Managed-package components carry a `NamespacePrefix`. Include it when reporting the
  rule so packaged rules are distinguishable from org-local ones.
- Inactive rules (`Active = false`) must be extracted but clearly marked. They do not
  fire, so they must not appear in the eval set.
- Developer Edition orgs allow ~15,000 API calls per day. Cache every describe and rule
  fetch to sqlite, keyed by org id, so re-running `scan` costs nothing.
- A field marked `nillable = false` in describe is required at the schema level.
  Business-required fields enforced by a validation rule will *not* show up this way —
  that gap is exactly the product.
